// REJECTS: Unexpected token 'fixture'. Valid alternatives: ['(', ':']
//
// A relation function mapping takes EXACTLY ONE source clause: `~func <descriptor>` naming
// an existing function, OR `~src <expression>` giving one inline. They are alternatives of a
// single rule, not two optional clauses, so a mapping cannot carry both.
//
// The diagnostic shows how the constraint is enforced, and it is not by a mutual-exclusion
// check: RELATION_SRC is one of the tokens `identifier` admits, so after the ~func arm has
// matched, the second clause is re-read as a PROPERTY named `~src` and the error lands on
// the expression behind it. A rewrite treating both as optional named clauses -- the shape
// the source text suggests -- accepts this and then has to decide which source wins.
###Mapping
Mapping fixture::neg::RelationFuncAndSrc
(
   fixture::neg::Person: Relation
   {
      ~func fixture::neg::personRelation():Relation<Any>[1]
      ~src fixture::neg::Db.PERSON->select()
      firstName: FIRST_NAME
   }
)
